      These #define constants correctly specify the RISC-V privileged architecture CSR addresses for mscratch (0x340), mepc (0x341), mcause (0x342), and mtval (0x343). The addresses match the RISC-V privileged spec and are the standard architectural numbers. No violation exists at this definition site — the definitions are accurate and complete. The question of whether a given hart actually implements these CSRs is a hardware-platform concern, not something these compile-time constants can or should enforce.
